{"id":"georgia-caucasus","title":"Georgia: Kazbegi and Svaneti","who":"Classic route · the Greater Caucasus by motorcycle","when":"June to September","vehicle":"Adventure motorcycle, 10–14 days","kind":"moto","color":"#b45309","summary":"From Tbilisi up the old Georgian Military Highway to Gergeti church under Mount Kazbek, then west to Svaneti, a valley of medieval stone towers, and on dirt to Ushguli, one of Europe's highest villages, under Shkhara. Wine, feasts and wild driving; afternoon storms in the mountains. The Military Highway past Gudauri closes for avalanche risk in winter and for floods in the Dariali gorge at times.","sources":[{"label":"Caliber.az: Georgian Military Road reopens after overnight closure","url":"https://caliber.az/en/post/georgian-military-road-reopens-after-overnight-closure"},{"label":"Travelogue: Georgia, ten days and Ushguli (August 2025)","url":"https://mdwdotla.medium.com/travelogue-georgia-3f39363773b3"},{"label":"BMW Motorrad: panoramic Caucasus routes","url":"https://fuelforlife.bmw-motorrad.com/en/travel/panoramic-caucasus-routes.html"}],"approximate":"A common loop; the roads are the router's choice.","km":921,"bbox":[41.7886,41.6936,44.8014,43.0613],"stops":[{"name":"Tbilisi","place":"Tbilisi, Georgia","at":[41.6935,44.8014],"text":"Sulphur baths, balconies and the old town under Narikala fortress.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/View_of_Tbilisi_from_Tabori_Church_2023-10-08-2.jpg/500px-View_of_Tbilisi_from_Tabori_Church_2023-10-08-2.jpg","page":"Tbilisi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Tbilisi_from_Tabori_Church_2023-10-08-2.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Ananuri","place":"Ananuri, Georgia","at":[42.177,44.6906],"text":"A fortress church above a turquoise reservoir.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Georgian_Fortress_Ananuri.jpg/500px-Georgian_Fortress_Ananuri.jpg","page":"Ananuri","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgian_Fortress_Ananuri.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Kazbegi","place":"Stepantsminda, Georgia","at":[42.658,44.6408],"text":"Over the Jvari pass to Gergeti Trinity church under the glaciers of Kazbek.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Gergeti_Trinity_Church_09.23.jpg/500px-Gergeti_Trinity_Church_09.23.jpg","page":"Gergeti Trinity Church","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gergeti_Trinity_Church_09.23.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Mtskheta","place":"Mtskheta, Georgia","at":[41.8463,44.7196],"text":"Back down to Georgia's ancient capital and its cathedral.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/View_to_Mtskheta_from_Jvari.jpg/500px-View_to_Mtskheta_from_Jvari.jpg","page":"Mtskheta","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_to_Mtskheta_from_Jvari.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Kutaisi","place":"Kutaisi, Georgia","at":[42.2597,42.6634],"text":"West across the country to the old kingdom of Imereti.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Downtown_Kutaisi_%26_White_Bridge_as_seen_from_Mt_Gora_%28August_2011%29-cropped.jpg/500px-Downtown_Kutaisi_%26_White_Bridge_as_seen_from_Mt_Gora_%28August_2011%29-cropped.jpg","page":"Kutaisi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Kutaisi_%26_White_Bridge_as_seen_from_Mt_Gora_%28August_2011%29-cropped.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Zugdidi","place":"Zugdidi, Georgia","at":[42.5072,41.8717],"text":"The start of the climb into Svaneti, past the Enguri dam.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/%E1%B2%93%E1%83%90%E1%83%93%E1%83%98%E1%83%90%E1%83%9C%E1%83%94%E1%83%91%E1%83%98%E1%83%A1_%E1%83%A1%E1%83%90%E1%83%A1%E1%83%90%E1%83%AE%E1%8